From 6071007be7fa016c7d3748e93f425676be3c3962 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:29:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: power up the USB PCS in usb_power_on()

USB power-off clears SW_PWRDN, but common initialization can return early
when the shared block is still in use. Set SW_PWRDN in USB power-on so
PCS can leave reset on the next initialization.

Adapt the common-block fix to the existing shared USB/DP lifecycle.

Source-commit: 1fd1e0452839b8699b5b71c83959461c7995672e
Link: https://github.com/TheMojoMan/oneplus-erhai-linux/commit/1fd1e0452839b8699b5b71c83959461c7995672e
Signed-off-by: nadelacruz-00 <323917690+nadelacruz-00@users.noreply.github.com>

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index cdcfad2e8..7d80727cc 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -3879,6 +3879,9 @@ static int qmp_combo_usb_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 	unsigned int val;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* The common block can stay initialized while USB PCS is powered off. */
+	qphy_setbits(pcs, cfg->regs[QPHY_PCS_POWER_DOWN_CONTROL], SW_PWRDN);
+
 	qmp_configure(qmp->dev, serdes, cfg->serdes_tbl, cfg->serdes_tbl_num);
 
 	/* Tx, Rx, and PCS configurations */
-- 
2.56.1

